<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=stirrup">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Transport and navigation</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stirrup</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 4th century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A stirrup is a light frame or ring hung by a strap from a saddle to hold a rider's foot, first known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under the Jin dynasty in the early 4th century CE. A tomb figurine of 302 shows a mounting stirrup and one of about 322 a riding pair; stirrups appear to have been in widespread use across China by 477. Central Asian invaders such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> brought them to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, where they occur in 7th-century Avar graves in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. By steadying the rider, they changed the tactics of mounted warfare.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stirrup.jpg" alt="Stirrup" width="320" height="345" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miguel Hermoso Cuesta · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caballo_Haniwa_Guimet_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>302 CE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Changsha, China</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Toe loops were used in India by the 2nd century BCE, some credit the Sarmatians, and a single iron stirrup from Mongolia is dated 243–405 CE.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/domestication-of-the-horse">Domestication of the horse<span>c. 2200 BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=stirrup">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
